meta {
  name: Concat - Mixed Stream Format Selection
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/concat/mixed?response_mode=stream&return_format=mp3
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  response_mode: stream
  return_format: mp3
}

body:multipart-form {
  request_json: {
    "segments": [
      {"type": "server_file", "source": "concatenation_test/01-sarah-audio.mp3"},
      {"type": "upload", "index": 0},
      {"type": "silence", "source": "(500ms)"},
      {"type": "server_file", "source": "concatenation_test/03-sarah-audio.mp3"}
    ],
    "export_formats": ["wav", "mp3", "flac"],
    "normalize_levels": true,
    "crossfade_ms": 250
  }
  uploaded_files: @file(./test-files/audio-sample.wav)
}

docs {
  # Audio Concatenation - Mixed Stream with Format Selection
  
  Generate multiple audio formats and stream a specific one, with alternatives accessible via header.
  
  ## Format Selection
  - **export_formats**: Generate multiple formats ["wav", "mp3", "flac"]
  - **return_format**: Choose which format to stream (mp3 in this example)
  - **X-Alternative-Formats**: Header lists URLs to other generated formats
  
  ## Query Parameters
  - **response_mode=stream**: Stream the file directly
  - **return_format=mp3**: Stream MP3 (alternatives: wav, flac)
  
  ## Response Headers
  ```
  Content-Type: audio/mpeg
  Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="concat_..._4files_sil1_fade250_leveled.mp3"
  X-Alternative-Formats: wav:/outputs/concat_..._4files_sil1_fade250_leveled.wav|flac:/outputs/concat_..._4files_sil1_fade250_leveled.flac
  ```
  
  ## Use Cases
  - Generate high-quality WAV + compressed MP3 for distribution
  - Stream MP3 for immediate playback, keep WAV for editing
  - Create multiple format options for different platforms
  - Archive in FLAC while serving MP3
  
  ## Format Characteristics
  - **WAV**: Lossless, best quality, ~10MB/min, editing-friendly
  - **MP3**: Lossy compressed, ~1MB/min, widely compatible
  - **FLAC**: Lossless compressed, ~5MB/min, excellent balance
  
  ## Advanced Features Combined
  This example demonstrates:
  - Mixed sources (server files + upload + silence)
  - Multiple format generation
  - Format-specific streaming
  - Crossfade transitions
  - Audio normalization
  
  ## Tips
  - Stream format based on immediate use (MP3 for web, WAV for editing)
  - Parse X-Alternative-Formats header to get other format URLs
  - All formats generated simultaneously for efficiency
  - Use appropriate format for target platform
}
